    "body": "@davidkna it did seem to help. It now seems to be down to 66ms, which still seems high. For reference, [zsh4humans](https://github.com/romkatv/zsh4humans) is lightning fast, there is no perceivable delay ever so I have no idea what the difference is there\r\n\r\nWhen I run `time git status` I get \r\n```shell\r\n❯ time git status\r\nOn branch main\r\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.\r\n\r\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\r\ngit status  0.01s user 0.02s system 5% cpu 0.537 total\r\n```\r\nso shouldn't I expect similar timing from starship?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
