    "updated_at": "2022-09-02T17:04:08Z",
    "body": "> Could some of this be improved if `exec_cmd` streamed command output instead of buffering it into a string? Maybe it can't be rendered asynchronously, but at least it can be processed into memory iteratively. Perhaps this would pipeline the [parsing](https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/modules/git_status.rs#L227-L233)?\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/utils.rs#L112-L116\r\n> \r\n> I'm assuming buffering is happening because the `CommandOutput.stdout` is type `string` instead of [`io::Stdout`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/struct.Stdout.html)?\r\n\r\nThat should be possible by using the `Command`-APIs directly (though timeouts should still be handled via `process_control`).\r\nCurrently, it waits for git to exit and reads stdout and stdin completely into a string buffer. Streaming may improve performance, but I don't expect it to be dramatic, though with some effort it might be possible to exit processing early in some cases.\r\n\r\n> https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/master/src/utils.rs#L88-L91\r\n> \r\n> I'm interested in learning more about the project. Is there documentation on the design?\r\n\r\nNot really, but `Contributing.md` contains some explanations.",
