    "body": "As a possible workaround, I recently changed my setup to use [gitstatusd](https://github.com/romkatv/gitstatus), a background daemon that tracks status and makes it available very quickly to shell prompts even with massive repos. \r\n\r\nIt makes various status fields available as env vars, which you can then further process as you like. Ultimately, I use the zsh gitstatusd plugin, wrap it in a shellscript to format how I like and export formatted env vars, and then display it in my starship using a the `env_var` module. Here's my relevant:\r\n- [starship config](https://github.com/junosuarez/rc/blob/dde8e343c3b51f5822ea49245525619837ba4f01/modules/prompt/starship.toml#L63-L80)\r\n- [git status formatter](https://github.com/junosuarez/rc/blob/dde8e343c3b51f5822ea49245525619837ba4f01/modules/git-status/profile.zsh)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
